* ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000001⟫

A ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000002⟫⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000003⟫⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000004⟫ is a lightweight thread managed by the ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000005⟫ runtime.

⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000006⟫

starts a new ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000007⟫ running

⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000008⟫

The evaluation of ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000009⟫f⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000010⟫, ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000011⟫x⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000012⟫, ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000013⟫y⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000014⟫, and ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000015⟫z⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000016⟫ happens in the current ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000017⟫ and the execution of ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000018⟫f⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000019⟫ happens in the new ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000020⟫.

⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000021⟫ run in the same address space, so access to shared memory must be synchronized. The [[⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000022⟫][⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000023⟫sync⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000024⟫]] package provides useful primitives, although you won't need them much in ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000025⟫ as there are other primitives. (See the next slide.)

